@{ Layout = "_LayoutPublic"; ViewData["Title"] = "Pricing & Commercial Model"; }
<section class="spx-page-hero"><div class="container">
  <span class="spx-kicker">Enterprise SaaS · pilot-scoped pricing</span>
  <h1>Pricing that maps to how a port actually scales</h1>
  <p>Smart Port is licensed against the three things that drive value and cost: berths under management, fleet vehicles coordinated, and ports deployed. Figures below are <strong>indicative ranges for a synthetic-data prototype</strong> — final commercial terms depend on deployment scope, integrations, security review and support. No live pricing, customer or partnership is implied.</p>
</div></section>

<!-- Licensing dimensions -->
<section class="spx-section spx-section--deep"><div class="container">
  <div class="spx-section__head"><span class="spx-kicker">How it's licensed</span><h2>Three pricing dimensions</h2><p>Most deployments combine a per-port platform fee with per-berth and per-vehicle metering — so a small fleet pilot and a multi-terminal rollout both have a clean line item.</p></div>
  <div class="spx-card-grid spx-card-grid--three">
    <article class="spx-product"><span></span><h3>Per berth</h3><p><strong>Indicative: R6k–R12k / berth / month.</strong> Control-room reasoning, execution plans, berth/gate/yard signals and emissions impact for each berth under management.</p></article>
    <article class="spx-product"><span></span><h3>Per fleet vehicle</h3><p><strong>Indicative: R180–R350 / vehicle / month.</strong> Driver companion seat, queue position, tap-to-check-in, fleet tracker presence and notifications for each coordinated truck.</p></article>
    <article class="spx-product"><span></span><h3>Per port (platform)</h3><p><strong>Indicative: from R45k / port / month.</strong> Tenant, SSO, RBAC, audit retention, connector framework and support baseline for each port environment.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

