<!-- Onboarding model -->
<section class="spx-section spx-section--deep"><div class="container">
  <div class="spx-section__head"><span class="spx-kicker">Implementation &amp; onboarding</span><h2>A four-stage onboarding model</h2></div>
  <div class="spx-loop">
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>1</span><h3>Discovery</h3><p>Map berths, gates, yards and fleet operators; agree the pilot success metric (idling, turnaround or reliability) and data-sharing scope.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>2</span><h3>Connect</h3><p>Configure connectors (TOS/IPMS, gate/SCADA, telematics, mobile API) against the existing adapter interfaces; validate field mappings.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>3</span><h3>Pilot</h3><p>Run with approved test drivers on a bounded scope; compare against baseline; tune deterministic thresholds and approval workflow.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>4</span><h3>Scale</h3><p>Security sign-off, operator training, SLA and runbook, then expand berth-by-berth and fleet-by-fleet.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- Integration narrative -->
<section class="spx-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="spx-section__head"><span class="spx-kicker">Connector-ready integration</span><h2>Built to ingest real port feeds</h2><p>The engine reads a normalised operational picture, so demo connectors swap for live adapters without rewriting the reasoning layer.</p></div>
  <div class="spx-feature-matrix">
    <article><h3>TOS / IPMS</h3><p>Berth schedules, yard occupancy, container dwell and appointment windows.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Gate / SCADA</h3><p>Gate throughput, lane status and weighbridge events for real backlog metering.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Telematics</h3><p>Fleet GPS and idling data complementing explicit driver check-ins.</p></article>
    <article><h3>AMI / energy</h3><p>Advanced metering and load-shedding signals for energy-driven disruption.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- Security posture -->
<section class="spx-section spx-section--deep"><div class="container">
  <div class="spx-section__head"><span class="spx-kicker">Security posture</span><h2>RBAC today, hardening roadmap to production</h2></div>
  <div class="sp-split">
    <div class="sp-split__text">
      <h2>What's in place now</h2>
      <ul class="sp-checklist">
        <li>ASP.NET Identity with 8 roles &amp; 12 fine-grained authorization policies</li>
        <li>Least-privilege surfaces: control room, fleet, driver and judge each see only their scope</li>
        <li>Account lockout (5 attempts / 15 min), 8-bit+ password policy, secure session cookie</li>
        <li>Security headers (nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY, Referrer-Policy, locked-down Permissions-Policy)</li>
        <li>Server-side AI only · human-approval gates · immutable decision audit trail</li>
        <li>Driver location captured on explicit check-in only — no background tracking</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="sp-split__text">
      <h2>Hardening roadmap</h2>
      <ul class="sp-checklist">
        <li>SSO / identity federation (OIDC / SAML) and MFA enforcement</li>
        <li>Durable, tamper-evident audit-log storage with retention policy</li>
        <li>Independent penetration test &amp; security review before production</li>
        <li>Data-residency confirmation and a driver-location privacy assessment</li>
        <li>Secrets management (key vault) and per-tenant encryption</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- Multi-tenant roadmap -->
<section class="spx-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="spx-section__head"><span class="spx-kicker">Multi-tenant readiness</span><h2>From single-tenant demo to multi-port SaaS</h2></div>
  <div class="spx-loop">
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>A</span><h3>Today</h3><p>Single-tenant demo: one synthetic port, role-based access, in-session audit trail.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>B</span><h3>Tenant isolation</h3><p>Per-port tenant boundary, scoped data, per-tenant configuration and branding.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>C</span><h3>Shared platform</h3><p>Pooled control plane with isolated tenant data, per-tenant connectors and audit retention.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>D</span><h3>Federated ports</h3><p>Multiple ports and fleet networks with cross-tenant analytics where data-sharing agreements allow.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

